<!-- RELIABILITY -->
<section class="reliability-section" id="reliability">
  <div class="section-eyebrow">Long-Term Stability</div>
  <h2 class="section-title">Years of Uninterrupted Operation</h2>
  <p class="section-lead">orange.Os servers run for years — not months — without a scheduled restart. Banks and telecoms trust it because it has never broken that promise.</p>

  <div class="reliability-layout">
    <div class="reliability-cards reveal">
      <div class="rel-card" data-step="SMF-01">
        <div class="rel-title">Automatic Service Recovery</div>
        <p class="rel-body">When a monitored service fails — DNS, NTP, network routing — SMF detects the failure, logs the event, and restarts the service automatically. Recovery happens in milliseconds, before human operators can even open a terminal.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="rel-card" data-step="ZFS-01">
        <div class="rel-title">Silent Data Corruption Prevention</div>
        <p class="rel-body">ZFS stores checksums for every block of data. On every read, checksums are verified. If a disk returns corrupt data — silent bit rot that would go undetected for months on other systems — ZFS identifies it and reconstructs the correct data from its redundant copy.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="rel-card" data-step="LIVE-01">
        <div class="rel-title">Kernel Patches Without Reboot</div>
        <p class="rel-body">Critical OS patches can be applied and activated using live kernel updating technology. Your server does not go down for maintenance windows. The kernel version advances, the server keeps running, your SLA remains unbroken.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="rel-card" data-step="AUDIT-01">
        <div class="rel-title">Complete Audit Trail</div>
        <p class="rel-body">Every privileged command, every service restart, every configuration change is logged with timestamps and user identity into tamper-evident audit records. Compliance requirements for banking and telecoms are met by default, not by bolted-on software.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="uptime-visual reveal">
      <div>
